
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A team of researchers led by Purdue University associate professor of philosophy <a href="https://www.cla.purdue.edu/directory/profiles/jp-messina.html">J.P. Messina</a> has been awarded a nearly $2.91 million in funding for its project, &#8220;The Neglected Safeguards of Liberalism.&#8221;</p>



<span id="more-27439"></span>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/jp-messina-jesse-crosson-brian-kogelmann-and-logan-strother-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-27440" style="aspect-ratio:1.774711710797741;width:693px;height:auto" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/jp-messina-jesse-crosson-brian-kogelmann-and-logan-strother-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/jp-messina-jesse-crosson-brian-kogelmann-and-logan-strother-300x169.jpg 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/jp-messina-jesse-crosson-brian-kogelmann-and-logan-strother-768x432.jpg 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/jp-messina-jesse-crosson-brian-kogelmann-and-logan-strother-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/jp-messina-jesse-crosson-brian-kogelmann-and-logan-strother-250x141.jpg 250w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/jp-messina-jesse-crosson-brian-kogelmann-and-logan-strother.jpg 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">J.P. Messina, Brian Kogelmann, Jesse Crosson, and Logan Strother</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The team includes co-principal investigators <a href="https://www.cla.purdue.edu/directory/profiles/jesse-crosson.html">Jesse Crosson</a> (associate professor of political science), <a href="https://www.cla.purdue.edu/directory/profiles/brian-kogelmann.html">Brian Kogelmann</a> (associate professor of philosophy and political science), and <a href="https://www.cla.purdue.edu/directory/profiles/logan-strother.html">Logan Strother</a> (associate professor of political science).</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an email, Professor Kogelmann writes, &#8220;The premise is that liberal democracies are in trouble, and traditional safeguards like formal constitutions haven’t held up as well as we might have hoped. We want to understand how safeguards that get less attention&#8212;like political parties, interest groups, universities, business firms, informal norms, Congressional staffers, and more&#8212;help sustain liberal democracy.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The centerpiece of the funding is a $1.99 million grant from the <a href="https://www.templeton.org/">John Templeton Foundation</a>. Additional funds are coming from Purdue University, the <a href="https://www.wabash.edu/stephenson-institute/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Stephenson Institute for Classical Liberalism</a> at Wabash College, the <a href="https://www.jackmillercenter.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Jack Miller Center</a>, and the <a href="https://theihs.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Institute for Humane Studies</a>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In addition to its research components, the project has an educational aspect. According to a <a href="https://www.cla.purdue.edu/news/college/2026/purdue-researchers-receive-over-2-million-to-study-overlooked-safeguards-of-liberal-democracy.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">press release</a>:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Beyond advancing academic research, a major goal of the project is to translate its findings into educational opportunities for students, educators and the broader public. The researchers hope to broaden civics education beyond constitutions and Founding documents to include the institutions and associations that help free societies function. The grant will support the development of a new civics textbook examining the neglected safeguards of liberalism, designed for use in advanced high school and introductory college courses. The textbook will bring together contributions from scholars across disciplines and provide educators with resources to incorporate these concepts into their teaching. The researchers also plan to host summer conferences for Indiana high school civics teachers, introducing educators to the research and providing instructional materials they can bring back to their classrooms.</em></p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There will also be events and research opportunities for students at Purdue.  &#8220;Universities have an important role to play in helping future officeholders learn the importance of liberalism-sustaining norms like toleration, respect for diverse perspectives and other tools like critical reasoning capacities that enhance citizen capacity.” said Messina.</p>



